# Build context for /libvox-sync, whose Dockerfile is built from this
# directory rather than its own: it imports /libvox-driver-koha, and a Docker
# context cannot reach outside itself.
#
# An allow-list, not a deny-list. Denying the heavy directories by name works
# until someone adds a new one, and the failure is silent — a slower build and
# a fatter context that nobody notices. Starting from nothing means a new
# module is excluded by default and has to be named to get in.

*

!libvox-sync
!libvox-driver-koha
!libvox-core

# Nothing below belongs in an image, and .env in particular must never be
# baked into one.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.env
**/*.egg-info
